      "writtenOn": "2024-05-13T20:50:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`sdp_state` is allocated here and only freed when `bta_dm_disc_reset` is called via `bta_dm_disc_stop()` which is only called with `BTA_dm_on_hw_off()`\n\n`bta_dm_discovery_cb` is never reset after `bta_dm_disc_init_discovery_cb` which is called by `bta_dm_disc_reset`, which is called by `bta_dm_disc_stop()`\n\nHence honestly the RAM is never freed after the 1st SDP search and you are not going to save much by using an unique_ptr\n\nBut if your next step refactor has some usage of this unique_ptr, I am ok, but otherwise, pure memory safing does not justify this change IMO.",
